{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn publish-(module|closure)\"'!|defn .*project-rows|lowering-profile'\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc | head -50; sed -n '64,105p' src/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:40:(def lowering-profile\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:55:   `:yin.vm/lower` under `lowering-profile`. A plain map, so it is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:65:   :yin.ledger/profile lowering-profile})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:177:   profile (defaults to `lowering-profile`). Returns nil when both steps\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:182:   (verify-derivation tree vector record lowering-profile))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:230:(defn project-rows\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:368:                      {:yin.semantic/code (mint tree-address sem ledger/lowering-profile)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:370:                       (mint sem h linker/stack-lowering-profile)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:372:                       (mint sem r linker/register-lowering-profile)}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:442:(defn publish-module!\n  #?(:cljd true\n     :cljs (exists? js/require)\n     :clj true))\n\n\n(defn- without-trailing-separator\n  \"The directory path with any trailing `/` removed, so the content log's\n   path is joined exactly once.  A path of only separators names the root,\n   which is preserved.\"\n  [dir]\n  (loop [s dir]\n    (if (and (pos? (count s)) (= \"/\" (subs s (dec (count s)))))\n      (recur (subs s 0 (dec (count s))))\n      s)))\n\n\n(defn content-path\n  \"The content log's own path inside the store directory:\n   `<dir>/content.jing`.\"\n  [dir]\n  (let [base (without-trailing-separator dir)]\n    (if (str/blank? base)\n      (str \"/\" content-name)\n      (str base \"/\" content-name))))\n\n\n(defn- error-text\n  \"The host error's own message, for the tail of a refusal.\"\n  [e]\n  #?(:cljd (str e)\n     :clj (or (ex-message e) (str e))\n     :cljs (or (ex-message e) (str e))))\n\n\n(defn- dir-refusal\n  \"Why `dir` cannot hold the durable content log, or nil when it can: a\n   path occupied by something that is not a directory, a directory this\n   process cannot write, or a directory that cannot be created.  Nothing\n   is opened here — the content log itself is opened later, and its open\n   failure is refused with its own reason.\"\n  [dir]\n  #?(:cljd (let [d (dart-io/Directory. dir)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
